  "measurement_method": [
    "Cost fixture uses the same original campaign character and river camera in archived baseline and current builds. The current test script is loaded by absolute path for the baseline.",
    "Preparation measures selection of RT through the first ready/active frame after the map has loaded. Same shared shader/asset cache; not cold game startup. One accepted run per variant.",
    "CPU-only scene.updates probe: 160 iterations per static/moving case, discard ten warm-ups. Moving case manually advances original walk animation and position. No rendering or ordinary game work is timed inside this bracket.",
    "Probe stops rendering before measuring, then disposes the scene; CPU-cached poses are not resumed on a mismatched GPU scene.",
    "Interleaved moving benchmark: three rounds, 35 settling frames then 90 samples per case, vsync disabled and no FPS cap. Baseline and optimized benchmarks run sequentially.",
    "Mirror uses 1280x720, 2x MSAA, engine viewport GPU measurements. RT uses 640x360 with approximate materials and GPU timestamps bracketing queued reflection work.",
    "Controller CPU uses process-priority 99-101 timestamps; excludes ordinary game and render-thread CPU work. FPS is the reciprocal of the median of three round-median frame times.",
    "Raw reflection readbacks compare all 230400 RGB pixels. Optimized and previous-build captures are identical; the current script control differs on three pixels by one 8-bit channel value."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Shared development machine; RT and Mirror have different resolution, AA, materials and scene coverage. Lower reflection overhead is not proof of a general FPS advantage.",
    "CPU vertex data and the full GPU vertex buffer still include hidden geometry. Fewer BLAS objects does not imply an equivalent total-memory reduction. First reveal may hitch.",
    "Morph deformation remains in GDScript and still rebuilds affected existing BLAS geometry. No acceleration-structure refit API is assumed.",
    "One original moving character; this does not qualify crowded combat, new GPUs or other operating systems.",
    "Existing water-only scope remains: one selected water plane, one reflection bounce, hard direct-light shadows; particles, shader-only wind, blended transparency, GI and in-place mesh/texture edits remain omitted.",
    "Existing engine SPIR-V diagnostic OpTypeAccelerationStructureKHR is not supported yet and private-Xvfb input-method warning remain. No script errors or functional failures in accepted runs."
  ],
